# fifo_gap_teardown_faulted_head: 0x1000 = 0 with a faulted head and two NOPs behind it: the teardown stops and drains the queue quiesced, which publishes the faulted head and everything behind it into the stamp slot before the mapping goes, and clears the fault mask: 0x102c reads 0 and 0x103c 0 (no FIFO). A FIFO enabled again on the same pages starts with fresh counts and no fault, and 0x1024 on it changes nothing; its first NOP (stamp 11) publishes.
{"op": "config", "ram": [["0x40000000", "0x4000000"]], "stamp_gpa": "0x40008000", "stamp_slots": 1, "watchdog_s": 30}
